# Scrollable Bottom Sheet — a gradient button opens a bottom sheet with a paging
# horizontal ScrollView of 3 pages (350/500/250pt); while scrolling, the sheet height
# is interpolated between page heights on the UI thread.
# What this test covers: open via the button, "Next Page" twice (sheet grows to
# 500 then shrinks to 250) and the third page's "Close"; swiping between pages
# by hand forwards and backwards (continuous height interpolation) and
# over-scrolling both ends; dragging the sheet down < 100pt (snaps back) and
# > 100pt (closes); closing via the backdrop tap; the toggle button pressed
# rapidly (open/close mid-spring); re-opening after the 500ms scroll-reset.
# Page buttons share a "Next Page" label across pages, so they are pressed by
# position (page1 y716, page2 y641, page3 y766).
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/scrollable-bottom-sheet"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 10000
wait 1000
press 201 437
wait "text" "Next Page" 3000
wait 800
press 201 716
wait 1000
press 201 641
wait 1000
press 201 766
wait 1200
# Swipe through the pages by hand.
press 201 437
wait 900
gesture pan 330 716 -260 0 700
wait 900
gesture pan 330 641 -260 0 700
wait 900
gesture pan 330 766 -200 0 500
wait 700
gesture pan 70 766 260 0 700
wait 900
gesture pan 70 641 260 0 700
wait 900
gesture pan 70 716 200 0 500
wait 700
# Drag the sheet down a little (snaps back), then past 100pt (closes).
gesture pan 201 600 0 60 500
wait 900
gesture pan 201 600 0 200 500
wait 1200
# Close via the backdrop.
press 201 437
wait 900
press 201 250
wait 1200
# Rapid toggling of the opener.
press 201 437
wait 150
press 201 437
wait 150
press 201 437
wait 1200
# Close from page 2 via drag, then reopen after the scroll reset.
press 201 716
wait 1000
gesture pan 201 500 0 250 400
wait 1200
press 201 437
wait 1000
press 201 250
wait 1200
wait "label=\"Close\"" 3000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\" id=\"xmark\""
wait 1500
